      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "Let $P=\\{{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,6].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}\\frac{({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})}{2}Δ{z}_{k}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}\\frac{({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})}{2}Δ{z}_{k}=\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=2$ and ${z}_{q}=6$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32=16.\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
